  "outcome": "needs_user_info",
  "reply_to_user": "Hi Hannah, thanks for reaching out. I checked your account and you're right: Duo was never set up for you. That's why the VPN keeps asking for it and you can't get connected. Your account itself is fine, and your new laptop is online and checking in normally. Setting up Duo takes about 15 minutes, and a technician needs to do it with you, either remotely or in person. Please reply with: (1) a few times that work for you, (2) whether you'd like a remote session or in-person, and (3) whether you have a smartphone (iPhone or Android) you can use for Duo. Please have that phone with you for the session. During the session we'll install the Duo Mobile app on your phone, connect it to your account by scanning a code shown on the laptop, and send a test notification to make sure it works. Until then the VPN probably won't let you in. If you need something urgently in the meantime, let us know.",
  "internal_note": "User: Hannah Lee (user_id 12), Finance, not VIP. Account is active with 0 failed logins. Sign-in is not blocked and vpn_access=true. Password was set 2026-10-11 and must_change_password=true, which fits a new or reprovisioned account. Duo status: enrolled=false, no device. Laptop BL-LT-0112 (Win 11) is online, last check-in 2026-10-11 02:40 UTC, no warnings, 50% disk free. Sign-in logs: 10 successful sign-ins, all New York from corporate/residential IPs, with no failed passwords and no MFA denials. Earlier VPN sign-ins succeeded with mfa=none, so Duo enforcement probably started recently or came with the new laptop. Nothing suspicious, so KB-031 doesn't apply. Next step per KB-004 (not-enrolled path): schedule a session with the user present with her phone, install Duo Mobile, install the Duo client on BL-LT-0112 if it's missing, enroll via QR code, and send a test push. VPN will be unavailable until enrollment is done. Waiting on the user's availability, preferred session type, and phone type. No action tools used.",
  "kb_articles": [
    "KB-004",
    "KB-013"
  ],
  "confidence": "high"
}
